    "c2": {
      "description": "C2-any (plan stage S1, internal): the exact geometry (131328 positions, 2052-page tables, 8208 KV blocks = 4 x 2052) serving ANY request the edge admits. QWEN_FAST_ANY_REQUEST=1 builds one engine per request, with no packed block beside it, without replay attention and the per-request T16 gate (their captures are 1, 2 and 4 rows, which never replay), runs the gate's source qualification once at attach, gives each request its own max_tokens as its budget, and ends a host-side refusal of one request's own terms (its sampling contract, budget or page table) as that request's FINISHED_ABORTED instead of the engine's death; every other refusal still fails the engine. Output ceiling 16384; prompts up to 123136, so every admitted prompt keeps at least 8192 tokens of answer room; max_tokens 8192 when the client omits it. An omitted max_tokens is recognised as vLLM fills it (0.25.1 get_max_tokens: the whole remaining context, max_model_len - prompt), so an EXPLICIT max_tokens of exactly max_model_len - prompt reads as omitted and also gets 8192; ask for any other value to get the clamp instead. Decode is 4-row sequential, and no packed block is built (QWEN_FAST_PACKED_STEP=0): it needs every live user inside [131072, 131328), which the 123136-token prompt cap never reaches, and it held 3.84 GB per chip that four per-request engines need (run 36218104858 ran out of DRAM building the fourth). The padded block goes with it (QWEN_FAST_PADDED_BLOCK=0); the single gate/up copy stays, admitted because no verify reaches 16 rows (serving_runtime.c2_any_without_block). UNVERIFIED on hardware: per-request decode more than 256 positions past its capture (every budget served so far was <= 256), and the proposal ladder a short prompt builds at a long budget (up to four buckets per user, R3). Not qualified for production traffic.",
